            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0060" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10641: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-05T11:00:00-04:00">May 5, 1941—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. Referring to the Department’s circular telegram of April 29, 10 p.m.,
                    Bolivian Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="10" xml:id="d47-f1"/> tells me
                    he has already indicated informally to Spanish authorities advisability of
                    refraining from actively supporting Axis Powers and he does not feel it would be
                    helpful for him to take further action individually in this matter.</p>
                <p>However he suggests that joint action would be more helpful and he is prepared to
                    consider such a plan if other Latin American countries are of similar view.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d47-f1" n="10" xml:id="d47-f1-content">
